v1.0.55 build 72: fix modal open animation jank via post-transition deferral

Researched via Playwright / web resources:
1. Modal open animation stutter is caused by heavy widget build +
   compositing overhead during the slide-up transition.
2. In booking manual, the parent form is heavy (5+ text fields, 2 image slots)
   which makes compositing even more expensive during route animation.
3. Deferred build via addPostFrameCallback was insufficient because it only
   waited 1 frame (16ms) while the transition takes 335ms.

Fix:
- sheet_picker.dart: _DeferredDatePickerSheet now listens to the route's
  animation status and only builds the heavy CupertinoDatePicker AFTER
  AnimationStatus.completed. During the 335ms transition, only a lightweight
  empty Container(color: cardBg) is rendered, eliminating compositing overhead.
- manual_booking_modal.dart: added FocusScope.of(context).unfocus() + 150ms
  delay when keyboard is visible before opening pickers, preventing concurrent
  keyboard-dismiss and modal-open animations.
